WEBVTT

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.810
Oh, you're here.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.750
Jeez, it's so cold.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.880
You should've used your key quicker.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.250
What's with that?

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.960
It's from Touko's exhibition.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.180
It ended today, so I took something they were using as a decoration.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.010
Did she get any customers?

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:24.960
Yeah.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.080
She found buyers for all the puppets she had on exhibit.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.910
It looks like I'll be able to get my pay this month.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.230
What were you doing today?

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.610
I actually went to school this morning.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:39.880
I see.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.620
Forgot I bought these at the vending machine there.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.920
Do you want one? It'd warm you up.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.370
I don't want something sweet.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.450
I see.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:55.200
But that's what makes it good.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.810
I changed my mind.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:06.980
I'll have a little.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.220
It's warm.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.380
<i>Like snow.</i>

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:52.320
<i>The white night when we first met, and the black umbrella.</i>

00:02:55.890 --> 00:03:01.900
<b>Kara no Kyoukai</b>

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:55.760
Let's go home already, Mikiya.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.150
She won't pay you for overtime anyway, right?

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.090
Yeah.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.790
After I put this away.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.240
What is this?

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:25.290
Oh, you bought another one of these things?

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.480
I didn't buy it.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.300
I just happened to meet it.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:32.350
Still sounds bad even if you try to put a romantic spin on it.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:34.300
Man, I'm hungry.

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:43.980
Shiki.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.230
Just go.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:50.060
She may eat someone if you let her be.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.530
Goodbye.

00:05:58.570 --> 00:05:59.920
Good job today.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:23.160
They have determined that the murderer is the same person who did the serial killings

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.580
and are continuing to investigate.

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:25.420
<b>Serial killings victim - 7</b>

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:28.900
There have been 7 murder victims so far in Mifune City.
<b>Serial killings victim - 7</b>

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.570
Combined with the murders that took place 4 years ago,
<b>Serial killings victim - 7</b>

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:31.900
this makes a total of 13 victims.
<b>Serial killings victim - 7</b>

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:31.920
this makes a total of 13 victims.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:35.960
People are starting to complain about the police's inability

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:38.010
to stop the continuous murders of this homicidal maniac.

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:41.790
The investigators are reviewing the records from back then and...

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.450
It's a homicidal maniac, Mikiya.

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:47.250
They must be calling him a homicidal maniac because there's been over 10 victims.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:51.110
But still, isn't calling him that going a little too far?

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:54.300
No, they're using it right.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:07:00.810
The one behind all this can't be anything but a homicidal maniac.

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:04.890
The culprit must be glad he's being called that.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.960
Homicidal maniacs don't need a reason.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:12.910
The victims were attacked by mere chance.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.820
That's why this guy hasn't killed people.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:19.920
This murderer hasn't killed anyone?

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:23.120
Slaughter and murder are different.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:26.050
Do you remember, Kokutou?

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:30.840
A person can only kill one person in their lifetime.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:33.870
Can only kill one person...?

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:38.460
It's fine.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.220
It's nothing.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:42.770
Anyway, let's eat.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:47.940
I heard that you took Azaka to a fancy Japanese restaurant after the Reien incident.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.400
Azaka...

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:54.970
And strangely enough, that restaurant's a place I've always wanted to go eat at.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:57.840
That was the first time I felt like killing Azaka.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:58.990
Guess I don't have much of a choice.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.340
I'm ready.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:02.890
C'mon, take me to any restaurant you want.

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:04.530
That's more like it.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:22.770
I'd say it's been about two or three days since they died.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:30.040
Judging by the torn off cross-section, I believe this was also done by the person who leaves leftovers.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.220
This is terrible.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:40.060
But as I've said before, considering the state of the corpses, it's unlikely that a human did this.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:42.510
I can only imagine something like an alligator doing this...

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:44.050
I found it!

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.030
Sleep here tonight.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.510
Okay.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.500
I'm heading out.

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:43.660
Okay.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:24.580
Touko.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:28.620
Can I leave early?

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:39.720
Are you going to go see Shiki again today?

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:49.420
What happened four years ago and now this killer...

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:57.430
Do you think it's Shiki?

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:01.860
I hear that due to the state of the corpse from last night's murder,

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:07.470
it's hard to determine the exact time of the crime. It's just like the murders from four years ago.

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:11.470
All we have are rough estimates of the date and time.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:18.580
And Shiki doesn't have an alibi during those times.

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:25.240
If we're just stating the facts, there isn't enough proof against it.

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:28.490
So you investigated it.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:32.010
But you look depressed.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:40.450
You must have a more fundamental question than her proof of innocence. Right, Kokutou?

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:43.110
That's right.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:48.570
The male personality, SHIKI, isn't inside of Shiki anymore.

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:55.530
She's been by herself ever since she woke up from that coma.

00:12:55.970 --> 00:13:02.100
Coincidentally, this also indicates that the personality called murder is no longer inside of her.

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:07.300
So your real question is this:

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:12.820
Doesn't this mean that Shiki has no more urge to kill?

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:15.710
I understand.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:20.090
But then, why would Shiki want to kill now?

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:23.050
It must be compensatory behavior.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:26.230
It's similar to Fujino Asagami.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:31.300
She can't feel her own life unless she's in contact with life.

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:35.340
Don't you think her method is a bit dangerous?

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:41.590
Look, if it bothers you so much, you just need to be with Shiki all day.

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:42.830
I wouldn't mind.

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:48.550
Breaking news, another victim of the serial killings?!

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:51.880
According to the information we just obtained,

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:57.350
another victim of the homicidal maniac was found in Mibukitachou in Mifune City.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:01.310
Another victim of the homicidal maniac was found.

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:03.560
According to a witness,

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:11.680
there were lots of bloodstains and scattered ankles and wrists, just like at the other crime scenes.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.910
The identity of the victim is still unknown.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.320
It hasn't been long since the person was killed,

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:17.870
so there's a possibility that the killer is still in the area and...

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.030
Hello? H...
so there's a possibility that the killer is still in the area and...

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:21.490
<i>I cannot answer your call right now.
so there's a possibility that the killer is still in the area and...</i>

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:21.830
so there's a possibility that the killer is still in the area and...

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:22.690
<i>Please leave your message after the tone.
so there's a possibility that the killer is still in the area and...</i>

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:28.910
<i>Please leave your message after the tone.</i>

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:41.770
Shiki!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:02.240
<i>Four years ago, Shiki told me that she's a murderer.</i>

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:05.030
<i>But that's not true.</i>

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.050
<i>She can't kill someone, no matter what.</i>

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:10.540
<i>She wouldn't be able to kill even if she wanted to.</i>

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:14.720
<i>That's what I've always believed.</i>

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:16.300
<i>I've believed.</i>

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:09.100
Kokutou, say something.

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:10.440
Kokutou!

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:12.630
I-I...

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:17.040
I don't want to die.

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:26.030
I want to kill you.

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.110
Why?

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.080
Fool.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:11.890
I did not wish for this collapse.

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.460
You can't kill me?

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:39.130
Appropriate if you're trying to kill to survive.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:43.030
But you're trying to kill so you can run away.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.410
Do not lower your own value.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:50.290
You belong to one person.

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:56.460
Live as one, and conclude as one.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:18:02.050
The spiral of conflict is the appropriate end for you.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.090
I...

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:12.770
Shiki.

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:18.070
Shiki!

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:26.720
It's too early to destroy that.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:41.340
<i>Back then, I decided to be with her instead of going home by myself.</i>

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:46.700
<i>I still don't know if that was the right thing to do.</i>

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:32.350
Kokutou.

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:41.640
<b>PAVILION</b>

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:54.530
<i>I came to this country because Souren Araya requested</i>

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:59.260
<i>that I return the memory that you lost in oblivion two years ago.</i>

00:22:00.240 --> 00:22:02.850
<i>I shall play back the grief.</i>

00:22:02.850 --> 00:22:09.000
<i>Even if you forgot it, the memory is actually recorded inside of you.</i>

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:17.930
<i>I cannot answer your call right now.</i>

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:25.810
<i>Please leave your message after the tone.</i>

00:22:29.350 --> 00:22:30.420
This is Kokutou.

00:22:30.730 --> 00:22:32.970
Guess you aren't back yet.

00:22:32.970 --> 00:22:35.270
Please contact me when you get this message.

00:22:35.270 --> 00:22:36.580
I'll call again.

00:22:37.510 --> 00:22:43.380
<i>February 8th, 4:33 PM.</i>

00:22:43.380 --> 00:22:46.470
<i>You have 17 messages.</i>

00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:18.340
Yo.

00:23:20.190 --> 00:23:22.950
Where have you been wandering about every night?

00:23:23.850 --> 00:23:26.600
Same to you. What are you doing here at this time?

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.680
Well, I came to this area to investigate.

00:23:29.680 --> 00:23:31.120
Oh, thanks.

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:43.180
You found a corpse in front of Ryougi's place three years ago, right?

00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:47.690
You know that the killer started again, right?

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:54.690
Did something happen?

00:23:55.820 --> 00:23:58.600
We found a clue about the killer.

00:23:59.610 --> 00:24:04.290
All the murders that took place this year occurred in the back alley of the business district.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:11.210
There are large streets around the murder scenes. So naturally, there are lots of people around.

00:24:11.780 --> 00:24:16.100
A person wearing a kimono is always seen there.

00:24:17.640 --> 00:24:19.600
Hey, Mikiya.

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:24.220
Have you been having any problems lately?

00:24:26.300 --> 00:24:28.480
No, I'm fine.

00:24:35.090 --> 00:24:35.920
What are these?

00:24:38.540 --> 00:24:40.050
Do you know what they are?

00:24:41.270 --> 00:24:43.230
The stamp is LSD.

00:24:43.570 --> 00:24:45.410
The leaves are marijuana.

00:24:45.880 --> 00:24:51.510
Over half the victims killed in the last week possessed them.

00:24:51.510 --> 00:24:52.630
These?

00:24:53.130 --> 00:24:56.520
The police still haven't figured out where they got them from.

00:24:56.520 --> 00:25:00.150
I guess they're being secretly spread among young people.

00:25:05.510 --> 00:25:10.180
It may be meaningless, but I don't have any other ways to look for Shiki.

00:25:10.950 --> 00:25:15.360
Anyway, I'm thinking of looking into the relationship between the murders and these drugs.

00:25:15.610 --> 00:25:16.770
I see.

00:25:17.210 --> 00:25:20.430
I may be taking a long time off.

00:25:21.460 --> 00:25:24.410
I don't mind,

00:25:24.880 --> 00:25:26.570
but don't overdo it.

00:25:36.320 --> 00:25:40.000
My name is Aozaki. May I talk to Detective Akimi?

00:27:29.130 --> 00:27:32.000
Young man, are you looking for something?

00:27:40.840 --> 00:27:41.810
Hold on.

00:27:42.330 --> 00:27:44.480
Go buy your drugs somewhere else.

00:27:44.480 --> 00:27:47.600
I have no business with people using the red ones.

00:27:47.930 --> 00:27:49.580
Please tell me something about this.

00:27:50.150 --> 00:27:50.930
Anything.

00:27:53.220 --> 00:27:54.900
Rain again?

00:27:54.900 --> 00:27:56.470
What a bummer.

00:27:56.470 --> 00:27:58.330
I can't work at all.

00:28:11.340 --> 00:28:12.530
Shiki.

00:29:47.450 --> 00:29:50.080
Go somewhere else if you want to play with drugs.

00:30:17.330 --> 00:30:18.490
All right.

00:30:18.490 --> 00:30:20.410
You want excitement, right?

00:30:20.410 --> 00:30:23.750
I'll make you guys feel as good as you want.

00:30:56.160 --> 00:31:04.600
More victims were found last night.

00:31:04.600 --> 00:31:11.130
A passerby found abnormal amounts of blood and scattered body parts.

00:31:11.130 --> 00:31:12.770
It's ready.

00:31:12.770 --> 00:31:15.290
How do you feel? Any better?

00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:17.140
I'm fine.

00:31:17.140 --> 00:31:19.200
It's starting to go away.

00:31:19.200 --> 00:31:21.350
It lasts for about four hours.

00:31:25.580 --> 00:31:27.640
You're so curious.

00:31:27.640 --> 00:31:31.020
You actually tried the drug that's hitting the streets right now?

00:31:31.020 --> 00:31:36.740
Based on the scene, it's assumed that four men were killed...

00:31:36.740 --> 00:31:37.130
The homicidal maniac again?

00:31:37.130 --> 00:31:38.670
They have announced that a person wearing a kimono was spotted near the scene of the crime.
The homicidal maniac again?

00:31:38.670 --> 00:31:44.340
They have announced that a person wearing a kimono was spotted near the scene of the crime.

00:31:44.340 --> 00:31:47.330
The culprit is someone wearing a kimono?

00:31:47.330 --> 00:31:48.620
What the hell?

00:31:51.790 --> 00:31:54.530
Mikiya, what happens if you use this?

00:31:55.710 --> 00:32:01.190
You only feel what Hansel and Gretel felt. I don't really recommend it.

00:32:12.710 --> 00:32:15.530
You haven't changed at all.

00:32:17.710 --> 00:32:20.050
Well, don't go too far.

00:32:26.120 --> 00:32:32.290
The police have decided to investigate this suspicious person wearing a kimono

00:32:32.290 --> 00:32:34.340
since this person holds the key to the incidents.

00:33:16.470 --> 00:33:17.950
I'm happy to see you.

00:33:19.040 --> 00:33:21.040
We met yesterday.

00:33:21.040 --> 00:33:22.430
Do you remember?

00:33:26.090 --> 00:33:27.350
Excuse me.

00:33:27.770 --> 00:33:28.930
I want to ask you something.

00:33:34.340 --> 00:33:36.570
Why were you looking for me?

00:33:38.190 --> 00:33:40.070
You're a woman, huh?

00:33:40.360 --> 00:33:41.970
That doesn't matter.

00:33:41.970 --> 00:33:42.570
Why?

00:33:42.810 --> 00:33:44.220
You've got the wrong idea.

00:33:44.220 --> 00:33:47.860
You're the only one in this neighborhood who doesn't sell that cocktail,

00:33:48.280 --> 00:33:51.460
so I thought you'd be able to tell me about it.

00:33:51.460 --> 00:33:52.580
Is that all?

00:33:52.880 --> 00:33:58.260
It's strange how all the dealers keep their mouths shut about that cocktail, isn't it?

00:34:00.310 --> 00:34:02.470
All right. What do you want to know?

00:34:05.450 --> 00:34:06.620
I see.

00:34:06.620 --> 00:34:12.340
So you're saying there's some connection between the people doing it and the killer, huh?

00:34:12.340 --> 00:34:12.890
Yes.

00:34:13.330 --> 00:34:16.520
First of all, why are you investigating this?

00:34:19.300 --> 00:34:20.800
Oh well.

00:34:20.800 --> 00:34:22.030
I'll tell you.

00:34:23.130 --> 00:34:26.790
Like they said on the news, the killer is the kimono person.

00:34:28.280 --> 00:34:30.720
I think it was after I met you...

00:34:31.090 --> 00:34:35.590
I saw four young guys fighting a girl in a kimono.

00:34:36.120 --> 00:34:37.300
You saw it?

00:34:38.110 --> 00:34:42.480
You say it's a girl, but on the news, they said that the killer's gender is unknown.

00:34:42.480 --> 00:34:45.940
How were you able to tell that it was a girl in the dark?

00:34:46.310 --> 00:34:49.700
Because even though I was far away, I could see the beautiful curves of her body.

00:34:49.700 --> 00:34:52.390
Wait, do you know her?

00:34:55.070 --> 00:34:57.640
I don't think you should get involved with her.

00:34:57.640 --> 00:34:59.020
She isn't normal.

00:34:59.440 --> 00:35:02.820
She was surrounded by four men, but she was going easy.

00:35:03.360 --> 00:35:04.410
Going easy?

00:35:04.410 --> 00:35:06.220
She didn't kill them.

00:35:06.220 --> 00:35:09.050
That way, she could slash them over and over.

00:35:17.740 --> 00:35:24.120
I've seen a lot of crazy people, but that's the first time I've seen someone like her.

00:35:27.790 --> 00:35:30.600
I'm sorry. You look disturbed now.

00:35:30.600 --> 00:35:35.650
Oh, the four guys who got murdered were cocktail users like you guessed.

00:35:36.900 --> 00:35:40.560
If you can, could you tell me a bit more about this cocktail?

00:35:41.060 --> 00:35:45.030
You still want to find the kimono girl after hearing all this?

00:35:45.030 --> 00:35:46.290
Please.

00:35:48.160 --> 00:35:49.450
All right.

00:35:49.960 --> 00:35:54.330
The cocktail you're talking about is the new one with acid and marijuana, right?

00:35:54.330 --> 00:35:55.260
Yes.

00:35:55.580 --> 00:35:58.940
That drug is too dependent and too strong.

00:35:58.940 --> 00:36:01.590
That kind of drug really destroys your body.

00:36:01.590 --> 00:36:06.970
That's why I don't deal that cocktail, nor do I approve of the Bloodchip.

00:36:07.230 --> 00:36:09.500
Bloodchip...

00:36:10.450 --> 00:36:12.510
What's the Bloodchip?

00:36:12.510 --> 00:36:13.470
You don't know?

00:36:14.110 --> 00:36:19.330
It's a superior cocktail for people who can't get enough even with the normal cocktail.

00:36:23.310 --> 00:36:25.480
A superior cocktail...

00:36:27.550 --> 00:36:30.050
Let me ask you something.

00:36:30.050 --> 00:36:35.890
Does this Bloodchip have the same stamp shape and red color?

00:36:36.230 --> 00:36:37.120
Yes.

00:36:37.510 --> 00:36:38.750
And...

00:36:39.730 --> 00:36:42.750
Are the edges stained dark red?

00:36:42.750 --> 00:36:45.290
Oh, so you do know about it.

00:36:45.290 --> 00:36:50.100
The ones with the stains are special ones that the boss made.

00:36:51.430 --> 00:36:54.140
Is that a well-known fact?

00:36:54.140 --> 00:36:55.160
Of course.

00:36:55.160 --> 00:37:00.060
But the Bloodchip dealer only deals with children.

00:37:00.060 --> 00:37:05.260
The bottom dealers know about it, but the higher dealers ignore it.

00:37:05.260 --> 00:37:08.480
They think that it's just child's play.

00:37:08.480 --> 00:37:12.300
That's why the cops still don't know about the Bloodchip.

00:37:13.250 --> 00:37:14.520
Thank you.

00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:15.930
That was helpful.

00:37:17.190 --> 00:37:19.490
Don't be too reckless.

00:37:19.490 --> 00:37:24.560
The dealer is a charismatic figure for the people who use the Bloodchip.

00:37:24.560 --> 00:37:27.250
It's like a new religious organization now.

00:37:30.090 --> 00:37:31.260
Oh yeah.

00:37:31.900 --> 00:37:34.140
Do you know the name of this dealer?

00:37:34.750 --> 00:37:37.230
Oh, you don't know?

00:38:04.710 --> 00:38:08.260
So you really did go to all the crime scenes.

00:38:08.960 --> 00:38:10.070
Yes.

00:38:11.020 --> 00:38:12.810
Did you find out anything?

00:38:15.490 --> 00:38:19.410
Nothing that the police could use as a base.

00:38:20.280 --> 00:38:23.690
Aside from the fact that the crime scenes are near each other,

00:38:23.690 --> 00:38:25.820
I don't see anything else that's common

00:38:26.650 --> 00:38:29.070
between these murders that started happening last year

00:38:29.070 --> 00:38:31.380
and the murders that took place four years ago.

00:38:31.810 --> 00:38:34.760
But, based on the investigating I've done up to today,

00:38:34.760 --> 00:38:39.120
I think they were all done by the same person. I don't know why, though.

00:38:39.360 --> 00:38:42.120
I feel the same way, but...

00:38:43.250 --> 00:38:44.040
But?

00:38:45.090 --> 00:38:47.700
No, it's nothing.

00:38:48.320 --> 00:38:49.150
Yes.

00:38:49.900 --> 00:38:52.500
Thank you for everything.

00:39:01.440 --> 00:39:02.730
<i>But...</i>

00:39:11.840 --> 00:39:15.660
<i>The incidents started in remote areas and moved closer to the business district.</i>

00:39:16.420 --> 00:39:19.330
<i>Forbidden things used to take place outside,</i>

00:39:19.780 --> 00:39:25.250
<i>but now, a deeper darkness lurks within the daily lives of good people.</i>

00:39:26.530 --> 00:39:30.990
<i>You never know when the new person next door to you could become a victim or an assailant.</i>

00:39:32.090 --> 00:39:38.120
<i>It's natural that the shadows grow darker as the city gets brighter.</i>

00:39:39.080 --> 00:39:44.300
<i>The darkness of the city grew deeper, and the darkness of the people grew even deeper.</i>

00:39:45.140 --> 00:39:52.160
<i>I don't know what you're looking for, but you can't illuminate your heart by yourself, Shiki.</i>

00:39:58.280 --> 00:40:02.670
<i>The deeper the night, the darker the darkness gets.</i>

00:40:03.620 --> 00:40:09.240
<i>I think I'm walking through the desolate town because I want to be alone.</i>

00:40:09.930 --> 00:40:15.610
<i>Or is it because I want to think that I'm alone?</i>

00:41:55.570 --> 00:41:57.270
At last we meet.

00:42:00.200 --> 00:42:04.110
Shiki Ryougi.

00:42:05.480 --> 00:42:06.830
I know you.

00:42:12.040 --> 00:42:15.080
I know you. You're...

00:43:02.540 --> 00:43:03.760
Huh?

00:43:04.150 --> 00:43:06.050
That's strange.

00:43:06.050 --> 00:43:07.920
Is that all you can do?

00:43:11.510 --> 00:43:13.350
Shiki Ryougi.

00:43:46.890 --> 00:43:48.440
Why...

00:43:49.760 --> 00:43:51.640
Why won't you do it seriously?

00:43:53.070 --> 00:43:56.380
You're completely different from how you were four years ago.

00:43:56.380 --> 00:44:00.410
You could've killed me just now if you wanted to,

00:44:00.930 --> 00:44:03.780
but you're not trying to cross the line.

00:44:04.170 --> 00:44:08.100
I need you so badly...

00:44:08.780 --> 00:44:13.290
I wanted to see you because I don't have much time...

00:44:14.450 --> 00:44:17.250
Everything was for you.

00:44:17.250 --> 00:44:22.570
How I killed people, how I left the corpses so you'd know it's me.

00:44:23.860 --> 00:44:25.800
What are you talking about?

00:44:26.530 --> 00:44:30.440
I thought you would remember what happened four years ago if I did this.

00:44:32.980 --> 00:44:35.830
But you kept ignoring me.

00:44:38.160 --> 00:44:41.310
Instead, it had a different effect.

00:44:43.520 --> 00:44:46.110
Yeah, a homicidal maniac.

00:44:46.110 --> 00:44:50.360
I didn't have a name, but society gave me this name.

00:44:51.710 --> 00:44:54.030
It's spot on.

00:44:54.790 --> 00:45:00.450
I was so happy that I met their expectations this past week.

00:45:00.450 --> 00:45:05.270
A homicidal maniac needs to kill people as people expect him to.

00:45:05.270 --> 00:45:06.420
Right?

00:45:08.460 --> 00:45:12.010
You should know, Ryougi.

00:45:12.930 --> 00:45:16.600
That's why you were jealous and looked for me.

00:45:17.640 --> 00:45:22.520
You wanted to become free quickly. So you wanted to find me, someone like you.

00:45:25.230 --> 00:45:27.460
Yeah, I understand.

00:45:27.460 --> 00:45:29.250
I understand.

00:45:31.110 --> 00:45:35.660
Because I understand you the most.

00:45:36.270 --> 00:45:42.030
You can't be fulfilled no matter what you do because you're going against your origin.

00:45:42.030 --> 00:45:43.770
There's no need to suppress it.

00:45:43.770 --> 00:45:46.950
You only need to honestly do what you want to do.

00:45:48.560 --> 00:45:50.350
I've told you before, right?

00:45:50.350 --> 00:45:52.180
I'm not interested in you.

00:45:54.090 --> 00:45:56.460
I just wanted to confirm.

00:45:56.920 --> 00:45:59.310
That's a lie, that's a lie, that's a lie, that's a lie!

00:46:01.000 --> 00:46:05.480
As proof, your eyes are always looking at my death.

00:46:08.200 --> 00:46:11.320
You don't need to bear it, Shiki Ryougi.

00:46:13.130 --> 00:46:16.970
You came because your desire told you to, right?

00:46:16.970 --> 00:46:20.080
You followed me here because you want to kill me, right?

00:46:21.610 --> 00:46:24.080
Come on, kill me.

00:46:28.390 --> 00:46:29.820
I see.

00:46:29.820 --> 00:46:32.950
So you're saying that's not enough to make you come back?

00:46:32.950 --> 00:46:35.650
Then I'll have to kill the reason.

00:46:37.730 --> 00:46:42.020
The one who's holding you back.

00:46:42.340 --> 00:46:46.020
Then everything would be over.

00:46:48.500 --> 00:46:49.670
Who...

00:47:00.010 --> 00:47:01.910
...is going to kill <i>who</i>?

00:47:15.810 --> 00:47:17.800
I knew it!

00:47:18.410 --> 00:47:22.430
I knew it!

00:47:23.370 --> 00:47:26.490
You're the real deal.

00:47:41.160 --> 00:47:43.610
It's so simple.

00:47:46.600 --> 00:47:49.750
I just need to get rid of what's hindering you!

00:49:44.180 --> 00:49:49.290
April 1995, I met her.

00:49:58.300 --> 00:50:01.550
May. Let me talk about her.

00:50:03.080 --> 00:50:07.040
I still go insane when I see her.

00:50:08.300 --> 00:50:13.180
I'm just looking at her, but I've gone completely crazy.

00:50:14.330 --> 00:50:17.070
My daily life is being invaded.

00:50:18.420 --> 00:50:21.230
A miraculous female student at my high school.

00:50:22.320 --> 00:50:25.780
I'm probably in love with her.

00:50:28.280 --> 00:50:32.130
<b>In front of school
In front of school
Broad Bridge
Broad Bridge
July. "I hate weak people".</b>

00:50:32.130 --> 00:50:34.430
She said that calmly.
<b>Broad Bridge
Broad Bridge
